# Cursor Build Prompt – Phase <PHASE_NUM>

## Goal

Implement **Phase <PHASE_NUM>** exactly as defined in `docs/tasks.md`.

## Inputs

1. `docs/brd.md` (Business Requirements Document with all specifications)
2. `docs/tasks.md` (Phase <PHASE_NUM> section with specific tasks)

## Critical: BRD Reference Checking

• **ALWAYS** check the BRD.md line references (e.g., §75-76) for each task before implementing
• Each task with a reference number (like §239, §387-407) contains specific requirements in the BRD
• **NEVER** implement a task without first reading the referenced BRD section
• The BRD contains the authoritative specifications - tasks.md is just the implementation checklist

## Hard Rules (mirror BRD constraints)

• Single-file isolation (no shared utils, no cross-imports between tools)
• Only allowed third-party libraries: `httpx>=0.27`, `openrouter`, `firecrawl`, `proxycurl`, `mailgun`, `snovio`, `phonenumbers`, `portalocker`, `publicsuffix2`
• All timestamps → ISO-8601 UTC (Z suffix)
• Deterministic UUIDs per BRD spec (uuid5 with NAMESPACE_DNS/NAMESPACE_URL)
• Follow refresh-policy logic and error-handling rules verbatim
• Respect concurrency limits (max_concurrent_requests)
• Use portalocker for file writes only during write phase

## Work Guidelines

1. **FIRST**: For each task, read the BRD.md section referenced in the task (e.g., §239)
2. **THEN**: Write code directly into the repo paths listed in `docs/tasks.md`
3. When you finish a task, tick its checkbox in `docs/tasks.md`
4. Preserve existing file headers, docstrings, and licenses
5. If _anything_ is ambiguous, **stop and ask** before coding
6. Implement unit tests for all new functionality (90% coverage target)

## Deliverables

• Updated source files for Phase <PHASE_NUM>
• Updated `docs/tasks.md` with completed checkboxes
• Unit tests for new functionality
• Single commit with descriptive message

## Completion Signal

Consider Phase <PHASE_NUM> complete—and stop—once **all** checkboxes in `docs/tasks.md` under Phase <PHASE_NUM> are checked and committed.
